findings.detail:
The player doesn't ragdoll (ragdoll_player off). The first-person camera rides the animated EyePoint through the knockdown, the ko_back pose and the get-up, still looking level along the old look, so it stares along the floor over the player's own body. The Spine, Hips and legs aren't on VIS_FP_HIDDEN, so the belly and belt draw as a big navy slab, and as the player falls the gray legs rise into view first.

During the get-up the eye rises from behind the torso, and the lens passes 1.7 cm from the player's own mesh. While the player is down, nothing but the HUD bar says what happened.

The test-room sparring dummy can KO Game-boy (17 clean jabs), so he will see this. Everything else on this path is correct:
- the player never blinks off;
- auto_revive brings it back after exactly player_revive_s;
- the logs are clean;
- KO'd while holding, the victim freezes for the hitstop and staggers away 0.27-0.77 m from the lens, and the hold view eases out with no pop.

